1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:01,855
Dinner.

2
00:00:01,875 --> 00:00:03,455
Mum is mid-sentence.

3
00:00:03,475 --> 00:00:05,165
Theo is mid-chew.

4
00:00:05,185 --> 00:00:06,605
The gravy is mid-air.

5
00:00:06,625 --> 00:00:08,425
Because you just lied.

6
00:00:08,715 --> 00:00:11,309
In this world, every lie freezes everyone

7
00:00:11,329 --> 00:00:12,760
except the liar.

8
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:14,299
For five seconds.

9
00:00:14,319 --> 00:00:16,990
You told Theo you didn't eat his chocolate.

10
00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:19,240
Five seconds is plenty of time to hide

11
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,076
the wrapper.

12
00:00:22,126 --> 00:00:24,054
At work, it gets even better.

13
00:00:24,074 --> 00:00:25,956
Did you finish the report?

14
00:00:25,976 --> 00:00:26,715
Yep.

15
00:00:26,865 --> 00:00:27,320
Freeze.

16
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:28,920
You don't finish the report.

17
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,527
You do eat his biscuit.

18
00:00:31,437 --> 00:00:32,576
Is this one yours?

19
00:00:32,596 --> 00:00:33,378
Yes.

20
00:00:33,528 --> 00:00:34,458
It's not yours.

21
00:00:34,478 --> 00:00:35,653
It's bigger.

22
00:00:35,842 --> 00:00:37,587
Lying isn't a sin anymore.

23
00:00:37,607 --> 00:00:38,978
It's a superpower.

24
00:00:38,998 --> 00:00:40,657
Five seconds at a time.

25
00:00:42,307 --> 00:00:43,662
Then Mira calls.

26
00:00:43,682 --> 00:00:45,556
Her course is going badly.

27
00:00:45,576 --> 00:00:46,436
Be honest.

28
00:00:46,456 --> 00:00:47,897
Was moving away a mistake?

29
00:00:47,917 --> 00:00:48,247
No.

30
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:49,509
You're doing amazing.

31
00:00:49,959 --> 00:00:52,210
And this time, something is wrong.

32
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:53,720
Mira is still moving.

33
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:55,260
She's waving at the screen.

34
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,758
You can't move at all.

35
00:00:56,778 --> 00:00:57,483
Hello?

36
00:00:57,503 --> 00:00:58,318
You froze.

37
00:00:58,338 --> 00:00:59,566
Did you lie to be nice?

38
00:01:00,116 --> 00:01:02,691
A kind lie freezes the liar.

39
00:01:02,726 --> 00:01:05,046
And only the liar doesn't notice.

40
00:01:05,066 --> 00:01:07,146
Which means everyone who ever lied to

41
00:01:07,166 --> 00:01:09,437
protect you froze in front of you.

42
00:01:09,457 --> 00:01:10,948
You just never saw it.

43
00:01:12,797 --> 00:01:14,793
On Sunday, you visit Mum.

44
00:01:14,813 --> 00:01:17,050
You ask the question you never asked.

45
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:19,317
Were you really okay, when I moved out?

46
00:01:19,337 --> 00:01:20,577
Of course, love.

47
00:01:20,597 --> 00:01:21,466
Never better.

48
00:01:21,916 --> 00:01:23,246
And Mum freezes.

49
00:01:23,266 --> 00:01:24,311
Mid-smile.

50
00:01:24,331 --> 00:01:26,028
You count all five seconds.

51
00:01:26,048 --> 00:01:26,608
One.

52
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:26,958
Two.

53
00:01:26,978 --> 00:01:27,383
Three.

54
00:01:27,403 --> 00:01:27,833
Four.

55
00:01:27,853 --> 00:01:28,603
Five.

56
00:01:28,970 --> 00:01:30,685
She's been freezing for years.

57
00:01:30,705 --> 00:01:31,945
Every phone call.

58
00:01:31,965 --> 00:01:33,131
Every goodbye.

59
00:01:33,151 --> 00:01:34,929
You don't have to be fine, Mum.

60
00:01:34,949 --> 00:01:35,885
...I missed you.

61
00:01:35,915 --> 00:01:36,696
A lot.

62
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:38,179
Nobody freezes.

63
00:01:38,769 --> 00:01:40,724
Would you rather hear a kind lie, or

64
00:01:40,744 --> 00:01:41,666
the truth?
